  "blocks": {
    "AGENTS.md": "<!-- surveyjs:start -->\n## SurveyJS\n\nNo SurveyJS package was detected in this project, so the full skill set was installed. These skills describe SurveyJS v3.\n\nThe SurveyJS agent skills are installed in `.agents/skills`. Read the skill that matches the task before writing or changing SurveyJS code — they carry the current v3 API and the mistakes to check generated code against:\n\n- [`surveyjs-brand-styling`](.agents/skills/surveyjs-brand-styling/SKILL.md) — Style a SurveyJS application so it matches a custom app design, design system, or brandbook\n- [`surveyjs-creator-customization`](.agents/skills/surveyjs-creator-customization/SKILL.md) — Embed and customize SurveyJS Survey Creator (the drag-and-drop form builder) in React, Angular, Vue, or vanilla JS\n- [`surveyjs-dashboard`](.agents/skills/surveyjs-dashboard/SKILL.md) — Visualize and analyze collected SurveyJS responses with SurveyJS Dashboard (the survey-analytics package)\n- [`surveyjs-form-json`](.agents/skills/surveyjs-form-json/SKILL.md) — Author, edit, or debug SurveyJS survey/form JSON\n- [`surveyjs-integration`](.agents/skills/surveyjs-integration/SKILL.md) — Integrate the SurveyJS Form Library into React, Next.js, Angular, Vue, vanilla JS, or jQuery apps\n- [`surveyjs-pdf-generator`](.agents/skills/surveyjs-pdf-generator/SKILL.md) — Generate PDF documents from SurveyJS forms with SurveyJS PDF Generator (the survey-pdf package)\n- [`surveyjs-response-extractor`](.agents/skills/surveyjs-response-extractor/SKILL.md) — Extract structured survey responses from scanned or photographed paper forms, images, and PDFs with SurveyJS AI Form Response Extractor (the ai-form-response-extractor npm package)\n\nEverything between the `surveyjs:start` and `surveyjs:end` markers is regenerated by `survey-cli 0.1.0` (`npx survey-cli@latest init-agents`). Put your own notes outside the markers.\n<!-- surveyjs:end -->\n",
    ".github/copilot-instructions.md": "<!-- surveyjs:start -->\n## SurveyJS\n\nNo SurveyJS package was detected in this project, so the full skill set was installed. These skills describe SurveyJS v3.\n\nThe SurveyJS agent skills are installed in `.github/skills`. Read the skill that matches the task before writing or changing SurveyJS code — they carry the current v3 API and the mistakes to check generated code against:\n\n- [`surveyjs-brand-styling`](skills/surveyjs-brand-styling/SKILL.md) — Style a SurveyJS application so it matches a custom app design, design system, or brandbook\n- [`surveyjs-creator-customization`](skills/surveyjs-creator-customization/SKILL.md) — Embed and customize SurveyJS Survey Creator (the drag-and-drop form builder) in React, Angular, Vue, or vanilla JS\n- [`surveyjs-dashboard`](skills/surveyjs-dashboard/SKILL.md) — Visualize and analyze collected SurveyJS responses with SurveyJS Dashboard (the survey-analytics package)\n- [`surveyjs-form-json`](skills/surveyjs-form-json/SKILL.md) — Author, edit, or debug SurveyJS survey/form JSON\n- [`surveyjs-integration`](skills/surveyjs-integration/SKILL.md) — Integrate the SurveyJS Form Library into React, Next.js, Angular, Vue, vanilla JS, or jQuery apps\n- [`surveyjs-pdf-generator`](skills/surveyjs-pdf-generator/SKILL.md) — Generate PDF documents from SurveyJS forms with SurveyJS PDF Generator (the survey-pdf package)\n- [`surveyjs-response-extractor`](skills/surveyjs-response-extractor/SKILL.md) — Extract structured survey responses from scanned or photographed paper forms, images, and PDFs with SurveyJS AI Form Response Extractor (the ai-form-response-extractor npm package)\n\nEverything between the `surveyjs:start` and `surveyjs:end` markers is regenerated by `survey-cli 0.1.0` (`npx survey-cli@latest init-agents`). Put your own notes outside the markers.\n<!-- surveyjs:end -->\n"
